  "id": "Compound::DB06292 - Gene::7363",
  "verbalization": "Dapagliflozin, a sodium-glucose transporter 2 (Sglt2) inhibitor, is linked to Ugt2b4 through a series of biological relationships that span multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Dapagliflozin, as part of the Sglt2 inhibitor class, binds to Ugt2b4, which is a key enzyme in drug metabolism. This connection is reinforced by the fact that both Dapagliflozin and Canagliflozin, which are structurally similar, share a common ancestor in the organic cyclic compound class and are classified as Sglt2 inhibitors. The observed relationship between Dapagliflozin and Ugt2b4 is not only direct but also indirect, as the drug's effects on other biological outcomes—such as vulvitis or haematocrit increased—indirectly point to its interaction with Ugt2b4. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Sglt2 inhibitors, through their metabolic effects, influence Ugt2b4 activity, contributing to the overall pharmacological profile of the drug.",
